# Line endings
#
# The repository stores LF, and checks out LF on every platform. Without this,
# core.autocrlf=true on Windows rewrites every file to CRLF on checkout, which
# produces phantom whole-file diffs the moment a contributor on Linux or macOS
# touches the same file. Indenture targets .NET, TypeScript, Python, Go and Java
# with CI on Linux containers, so LF everywhere is the only consistent choice.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts: cmd.exe and PowerShell are the exceptions that want CRLF.
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf
*.psm1  text eol=crlf
*.sln   text eol=crlf

# Must be LF regardless of platform — a CRLF shebang line breaks the interpreter.
*.sh    text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.dockerfile    text eol=lf
gradlew         text eol=lf

# Binary — never convert, never diff as text.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.dll   binary
*.exe   binary
*.snk   binary
*.pfx   binary
*.avro  binary

# Generated artifacts: keep them out of diffs and language stats.
docs/api/openapi.v1.json  linguist-generated=true
